  - case_id: manual.audit.math.integer-scale-boundary
    contract: result-sequence
    difference_summary: result sequence
    rationale: "Primary review: accept only this x86_64 GNU/Linux five-result ldexp/scalbln boundary witness. tq uses deterministic safe saturating exponent conversion and maps NaN to zero, instead of reproducing the C wrapper's out-of-range floating-to-integer conversion. This is not rounding: oversized and NaN exponents can produce finite maximum or 2 where this jq produces zero. Such scripts are not interchangeable. In-range finite exponents remain exact obligations. Reconsider after implementation if a portable defined contract or safe-library conversion justifies a change, and remeasure on changed targets/references."
